{
 "record": "audio record \u2014 phase 17, JOB SOA01-AB-1 (A/B voice production). Three programmes over the piece bed, one per specimen. COMPARISON DESIGN: the transcript A/B (t1-clone vs t2-clone) differs ONLY in transcript \u2014 same voice (the clone), same chain, same bed; the voice A/B (t1-clone vs t1-default) differs ONLY in voice \u2014 same transcript (V1, the phase-16 recommendation), same pause map, same chain, same bed.",
 "fit_standard": "The branch fit standard (phase 11/14): silence-cluster-merge trims (silencedetect -45 dB, min silence 0.25 s, clusters merged across non-silent gaps < 0.35 s, 0.05 s pads); absolute starts LOCKED from the measured fitted durations + the candidate pause map (phase 16); fitted_end + planned gap = next start by construction \u2014 no overlaps (the VOICE FIT RULE). No atempo was needed on any line: each programme windows derive from its own takes.",
 "chain": "Per-stem: acompressor (threshold -16 dB, ratio 3, attack 2 ms, release 120 ms) -> measured scalar toward -13.8 LUFS -> alimiter LAST. Stems at the locked starts; bed (cited asset, loop-extended with a 3 s crossfade to the programme length) at a single measured scalar 13 dB under the voice mix, continuous \u2014 the bed never gates; two-pass loudnorm master to I=-14 / TP=-1.5. Every master is verified by measurement on the delivered file.",
 "chain_deviations_from_phase_14": [
  "The limiter runs with level=0 (auto-level OFF) and ceiling 0.70, LAST in the stem chain. Root cause found for register R-8: ffmpeg alimiter auto-level defaults ON and re-normalizes after limiting, silently defeating the cap (measured: a stem limited at 0.80 with defaults peaks at -0.0 dBFS; with level=0 it peaks at -1.9 dB, the cap holding). The phase-14 chain as written could not have capped as intended in this environment; its delivered stems are a matter of its own record.",
  "With a working ceiling, two scalar iterations land the stems at -14.3..-15.7 LUFS rather than the -13.8 target (the limiter shaving on these peaky takes converges slowly: ~+0.45 dB measured per +1 dB of scalar). The stem spread within a programme is <= 1.4 dB and every MASTER measures inside the band \u2014 the delivered artefact carries the standard, per the guarantee-by-construction rule: properties are verified on the delivered files, below."
